# What is and is not tracked, and why.
#
# This began as the stock Expo template ignore file, which assumes `android/`
# is regenerated by `expo prebuild` and therefore disposable. That assumption
# does not hold here: this project's android/ folder is hand-edited (the NDK
# path fix, the release signing config, and the Chaquopy setup to come), and it
# is the part most likely to need restoring after a failed experiment. Ignoring
# it would leave the repository useless for exactly the situation it exists
# for, so `/android` and `/ios` have been removed from this file.

# --- dependencies, rebuildable from a manifest -------------------------------
node_modules/
backend/.venv/
# A second venv pinned to the versions available on ANDROID (Python 3.10,
# scikit-learn 1.3.2, scipy 1.8.1, pandas 2.1.3, numpy 1.23.3). Training and
# testing run against it so that what is measured on the laptop is what the
# phone actually executes. Rebuildable; see backend/requirements-device.txt.
backend/.venv-device/

# --- build output ------------------------------------------------------------
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/.gradle/
android/.cxx/
android/app/.cxx/
modules/*/android/build/
*.apk
*.aab

# --- Expo --------------------------------------------------------------------
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
.metro-health-check*

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- PERSONAL DATA -----------------------------------------------------------
# The user's own measured screen time, unlock counts, notification counts and
# sleep estimates. This is the one genuinely private thing in the project, and
# it is excluded even from a local-only repository: a repository is a safety
# net for code, and personal data in git history makes the project awkward to
# ever share.
#
# Excluding it costs little, because the phone keeps its own durable copy of
# every captured day and re-uploads anything the backend is missing.
backend/data/*.db
backend/data/*.db-shm
backend/data/*.db-wal

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env*.local
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision

# --- editor / OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

example

# --- NOTE: backend/ and android/ have their own .gitignore files -------------
# They are the authority for their own trees, and their exclusions are
# deliberate rather than accidental:
#
#   backend/data/raw/*          the Kaggle datasets are licensed by their
#                               publishers, so they are downloaded rather than
#                               redistributed. See backend/README.md.
#
#   backend/app/ml/artifacts/*  trained models are BUILD OUTPUT. Regenerating
#                               them from the training scripts guarantees the
#                               models match the code that produced them; a
#                               committed model can silently drift from it.
#
# One exception is made, in android/.gitignore: local.properties is normally
# machine-local and ignored, but this project's copy carries the ndk.dir fix
# without which the C++ link fails with roughly 300 undefined libc++ symbols,
# together with the full diagnosis of why. Losing that is precisely the
# regression this repository guards against. Revisit if the project ever gains
# a remote or a second machine.
